# Inspera Core

Portable Windows PowerShell 5.1 toolkit. User docs: [README.md](../../README.md).

## Dev workflow

| Task | WSL | Windows |
|---|---|---|
| Edit code | Yes | Yes |
| Run tests | `./test.sh` | `.\test.ps1` or `test.cmd` |
| Run toolkit / diagnose real logs | No | Native |
| Build release (`build.cmd`) | No | Required |

## Layout

- Source: `lib/`, `data/`, entry `*.ps1`
- Generated: `dist/InsperaExamHelper/` — never hand-edit; rebuild after source changes
- Tests: `tests/` with fixtures in `tests/fixtures/`

## Changelog

- **Always** update [CHANGELOG.md](../../CHANGELOG.md) in the same change when behavior, user-facing copy, developer workflow, or shipped data changes
- Add entries under `## [Unreleased]` using `Added`, `Changed`, `Fixed`, or `Removed` — do not wait for a release bump
- Skip only trivial edits with no user or maintainer impact (typos, comments, refactors with identical behavior)

## Subagent delegation

- **Direct edits** for single-function or single-file changes
- **`explore`** when tracing a failure key across LogParser → ErrorCatalog → SystemChecks, or touching 3+ modules
- **`shell`** to run `./test.sh` after `lib/LogParser/` or `lib/SystemChecks/` changes
- **No subagents** for README wording, ErrorCatalog copy, or blocklist JSON alone
- **Parallel** subagents only for independent research; same-file changes stay sequential
